 I have found an inconsistency in Omega that is annoying.  If you are placed
on the tactical map with a creature beside you, the monsters seems to get a
lot of actions before you have the chance to do anything.  (I have seen 
monsters move 6 to 8 times or more)  If you appear without a monster beside 
you, they seem to get no extra actions, they don't seem to do anything until
after you have moved.  I tried looking through the code for this, but
I was not able to follow what was happening at the start of a tactical.
(I have had a couple of characters killed because of the "feature" or
bug, whichever it may be.  It is annoying to have your character killed
by repeated free attacks from a monster that he could have killed in
one or two blows.)
  
(The actual count is now 3 characters dead due to this,  the latest one
 got poisonned by a Ninja(genjin) and died of poisonning without getting
 one action in the tactical, he didn't even get a chance to look at what
 all was on the screen (ie x command).)

